<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How does the Grayson County Safe Room Rebate work?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">The Grayson County Office of Emergency Management provides a 50% matching rebate up to $3,000 for approved FEMA-certified storm shelter installations. Applications must be submitted and approved before installation begins.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Are above-ground safe rooms as safe as underground shelters?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Yes. When engineered and anchored in accordance with FEMA P-320 and ICC-500 standards, above-ground steel safe rooms are impact-tested to withstand direct 250 mph EF5 tornado winds and flying debris missile strikes.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How long does installation take?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Most residential above-ground safe rooms and in-garage floor shelters are installed in a single day (typically 4 to 6 hours). Outdoor underground concrete units typically require 1 to 2 days including excavation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do I need a building permit in Sherman or Denison?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Yes. The City of Sherman and City of Denison require building permits and final anchor inspections for storm shelter installations. We handle the permit paperwork on your behalf.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What happens if debris blocks the shelter door?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">All our safe rooms feature inward-swinging steel emergency escape doors with heavy internal sliding deadbolts, as well as secondary emergency air vents and multi-point emergency release latches.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;box-shadow:0 3px 12px rgba(10,61,92,0.06);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How much does a certified storm shelter cost in North Texas?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#5A6B76;margin:0;">Standard residential safe rooms range from $4,500 to $9,500 depending on dimensions and capacity (typically 4 to 12 person capacity). With the $3,000 county rebate, net homeowner costs can be as low as $2,250.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

